Question: Create a service performance report showing service name, total patients admitted, and a performance category based on the following:
'Excellent' if avg satisfaction >= 85, 'Good' if >= 75, 'Fair' if >= 65, otherwise 'Needs Improvement'. 
  Order by average satisfaction descending.

SELECT service,
COUNT(patients_admitted) AS total_patients_admitted,
ROUND(AVG(patients_satisfaction),2) AS Avg_satisfaction_score,
CASE 
	WHEN AVG(patients_satisfaction) >= 85 THEN 'Excellent'
	WHEN AVG(patients_satisfaction) >= 75 THEN 'Good'
	WHEN AVG(patients_satisfaction) >= 65 THEN 'Fair'
  ELSE 'Needs Improvement'
END AS service_performance_report
FROM services_weekly
GROUP BY service
ORDER BY avg_satisfaction_score DESC;
